#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Tidy up after a finished, archived run, without making a restore harder.

usage:
  python3 cleanup MANIFEST [--yes] [--json] [--history-dir DIR]

Without --yes it prints the plan and changes nothing (it never fetches; git
status runs with --no-optional-locks). The plan lists each run-owned item
with action remove or keep and the reason, the foreign items under
worktree_root it will leave, and the steps for the feature branch. With
--yes it first writes the restore point, then removes.

Preconditions (otherwise it refuses, exit 3, and changes nothing):
- the run is archived: index.json in the history dir (--history-dir DIR,
  else _history.history_dir()) has an entry for its _history.run_key, and
  that entry's folder exists;
- no active-run marker for its run_id is listed by
  bash <skill_dir>/scripts/active-run list (a marker means the run can still
  be resumed; a list that fails is a refusal too);
- with --yes only: cleanup takes the run's launch lock, as a resume of the
  run does (active-run acquire <run_id> <manifest>). A lock another session
  holds (a resume or another cleanup) is a refusal. Then, in git mode, it
  takes the checkout lock of the main checkout for the run (as setup does,
  through _locks.checkout_lock), so no other run's setup can switch it
  meanwhile; a checkout another live run holds is a refusal naming that run,
  and so is an unreadable or malformed checkout lock. Both locks are given
  back when cleanup ends, whatever happened (active-run release <run_id>
  --remove --owner <token>, which also removes the marker acquire wrote and
  the run's checkout locks); when that fails, cleanup warns on stderr and
  names active-run remove <run_id> --takeover, and its exit code stays.
  Shadow mode takes no checkout lock. Without --yes no lock is taken.

Run-owned items:
- <worktree_root>/lane-<id> for each manifest lane, on branch pl-<run_id>-<id>;
- in shadow mode, <worktree_root>/feature on repo.branch;
- the branches pl-<run_id>-<id> and repo.branch.
A worktree path counts only when git worktree list --porcelain shows it with
that branch and its git rev-parse --git-common-dir resolves to the repo's.
Anything else directly under worktree_root is listed in foreign with reason
"not owned by this run" and left in place. refs/parallel-lanes/<run_id>/ refs
are always kept.

The restore point is a new folder <run folder>/cleanup/<YYYYMMDDTHHMMSSZ>/,
made with os.mkdir; when it exists, -2, -3, ... are tried, so an existing
restore point is never reused or written into. PL_CLEANUP_STAMP, when set,
replaces the UTC timestamp (for tests). It holds, written in this order:
- refs.json: {"<ref>": "<sha>"} for the run-owned branches and every ref
  under refs/parallel-lanes/<run_id>/ that exists;
- run.bundle: git bundle create of those refs, checked with git bundle verify;
- restore.md: for each ref, git fetch <bundle> <ref>:<ref> (the bundle's
  absolute path), and a git worktree add line for each worktree to be removed.
  It is written last, so a folder without it is not a usable restore point.
In shadow mode every repo command uses --git-dir=<repo.git_dir>; in git mode
-C <repo.root>.

Removal (--yes, after the restore point), in this order; an item that
cannot be removed safely is kept and named with the reason:
1. run-owned worktrees the plan marks remove (clean and unlocked), with
   git -c status.showUntrackedFiles=all worktree remove (which itself
   refuses a dirty or locked worktree). Clean means git status --porcelain
   --untracked-files=all prints nothing: untracked files count even when
   Git's configuration hides them, and ignored files do not count. Ignored
   files do not keep a worktree: git worktree remove deletes them with it
   (build output, node_modules, an ignored .env), so copy any ignored file
   still needed before --yes. A
   worktree whose git status fails, or whose HEAD cannot be read, is kept.
   Right before each removal it is checked again, with a fresh git
   worktree list: it is still a run-owned worktree on its branch, it is
   not locked, its HEAD is still the planned head, and it is still clean.
   Otherwise it is kept with "changed after the plan (<what changed>); run
   cleanup again", and so is its planned branch;
2. lane branches the plan marks remove, with git branch -d (git mode only),
   each only while its tip is still the planned sha; otherwise it is kept
   with "moved after the plan; run cleanup again", or named with "deleted
   after the plan; nothing left to delete" when it no longer exists;
3. the feature branch (git mode only). It stops at the first failed
   condition, leaving the checkout and the branch as they are:
   - the main checkout is on repo.branch and clean (as in 1: untracked
     files count even when Git's configuration hides them, ignored files
     do not, and a git status that fails keeps the branch);
   - base_ref is a local branch with an upstream;
   - git fetch <remote> <upstream branch> succeeds within 120 s (with
     GCM_INTERACTIVE=never and no terminal prompt; on a timeout its process
     tree is killed);
   - repo.branch is an ancestor of the fetched tip (the PR is merged);
   - base_ref is an ancestor of the fetched tip (a fast-forward);
   - repo.branch is still at the planned sha (otherwise "moved after the
     plan; run cleanup again", or "deleted after the plan; nothing left to
     delete" when it no longer exists).
   Then git switch <base_ref>, git merge --ff-only <fetched tip>,
   git branch -d <repo.branch>;
4. worktree_root, with rmdir, only when it is empty.
Shadow mode removes the lane worktrees and <worktree_root>/feature, and
keeps every branch and the shadow repo. Foreign items under worktree_root
and refs/parallel-lanes/<run_id>/ refs are always kept. It never uses
--force or branch -D, never deletes a remote branch, never makes a merge
commit, resets or rebases, and never touches the manifest, the ledger or
the history folder (other than writing the restore point).

Output: the plan, as text or (--json) one JSON object:
  {"run_id", "mode", "run_folder",
   "worktrees": [{"path", "branch", "head", "action", "reason"}],
   "branches": [{"branch", "sha", "action", "reason"}],
   "feature_steps": [...], "refs": [{"ref", "sha", "action", "reason"}],
   "foreign": [{"path", "reason"}], "restore_point": <path or null>}
A worktree's head is its git rev-parse HEAD when the plan was made (null
when it cannot be read; the worktree is then kept).
With --yes the object also has "removed" and "kept": lists of
  {"kind", ..., "reason"}, where kind is worktree (with path, branch),
  branch (branch, sha), ref (ref, sha), path (a foreign item under
  worktree_root), worktree_root (path) or shadow_repo (path).
The text form of --yes lists removed, kept with reasons, and the restore
point. Paths use '/' separators (C:/... on Windows).

Exit 0 when done or planned (kept items included); 1 when a git command
needed for the plan fails (nothing changed); 2 on a usage error or an
unreadable manifest or index; 3 when refused (nothing changed); 4 when the
restore point could not be written or verified (nothing removed).
"""

import argparse
import json
import os
import re
import shlex
import subprocess
import sys
import time

sys.dont_write_bytecode = True
sys.path.insert(0, os.path.dirname(os.path.realpath(__file__)))
import _doctor  # noqa: E402
import _history  # noqa: E402
import _locks  # noqa: E402
import _shell  # noqa: E402

SCRIPTS = os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__))
# Variables that would point git at another repo than the one named.
GIT_REDIRECTS = ("GIT_DIR", "GIT_WORK_TREE", "GIT_INDEX_FILE",
                 "GIT_OBJECT_DIRECTORY", "GIT_COMMON_DIR")
ENV = {k: v for k, v in os.environ.items() if k not in GIT_REDIRECTS}
# git fetch must fail rather than wait for a password nobody types.
ENV["GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT"] = "0"
# How long git fetch may take before cleanup keeps the feature branch.
FETCH_TIMEOUT_S = 120
STAMP = re.compile(r"^[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._-]*$")
NOT_OWNED = "not owned by this run"
# The reason a branch whose tip is not the planned one is kept.
MOVED = "moved after the plan; run cleanup again"
# The reason given for a planned branch that no longer exists.
GONE = "deleted after the plan; nothing left to delete"
# The cleanliness check: every untracked file counts, even when Git's
# configuration (status.showUntrackedFiles) hides them; ignored files do not.
STATUS = ["--no-optional-locks", "status", "--porcelain", "--untracked-files=all"]


class Failure(Exception):
    def __init__(self, code, message):
        super().__init__(message)
        self.code = code


def run_git(args, cwd_args=()):
    return subprocess.run(["git", *cwd_args, *args], capture_output=True, text=True,
                          encoding="utf-8", errors="surrogateescape", env=ENV)


def slash(p):
    return p.replace("\\", "/")


def same_place(a, b):
    return os.path.normcase(os.path.realpath(a)) == os.path.normcase(os.path.realpath(b))


def load_manifest(path):
    try:
        native = _shell.native_path(path)
    except _shell.BashNotFound as e:
        raise Failure(2, str(e))
    try:
        with open(native, encoding="utf-8") as f:
            m = json.load(f)
    except (OSError, UnicodeDecodeError, ValueError) as e:
        raise Failure(2, "cannot read manifest " + path + ": " + str(e))
    if not isinstance(m, dict):
        raise Failure(2, "manifest must be a JSON object")
    repo = m.get("repo")
    if not isinstance(repo, dict) or repo.get("mode") not in ("git", "shadow"):
        raise Failure(2, "manifest repo.mode must be git or shadow")
    keys = ("root", "base_ref", "branch", "worktree_root", "ledger_dir")
    keys += ("git_dir",) if repo["mode"] == "shadow" else ()
    for key in keys:
        if not isinstance(repo.get(key), str) or not repo[key]:
            raise Failure(2, "manifest repo." + key + " must be a non-empty string")
    run_id = m.get("run_id")
    if not isinstance(run_id, str) or not re.fullmatch(r"[a-z0-9-]+", run_id):
        raise Failure(2, "manifest run_id must use only a-z, 0-9 and -")
    lanes = m.get("lanes")
    if not isinstance(lanes, list) or not all(
            isinstance(lane, dict) and isinstance(lane.get("id"), str) and lane["id"] for lane in lanes):
        raise Failure(2, "manifest lanes must be a list of objects with an id")
    return m


class Repo:
    """The run's repo: its paths in the native form, and git against it."""

    def __init__(self, m):
        repo = m["repo"]
        self.mode = repo["mode"]
        try:
            self.root = _shell.native_path(repo["root"])
            self.worktree_root = _shell.native_path(repo["worktree_root"]).rstrip("/\\")
            self.git_dir = _shell.native_path(repo["git_dir"]) if self.mode == "shadow" else None
        except _shell.BashNotFound as e:
            raise Failure(2, str(e))
        self.prefix = ["--git-dir=" + self.git_dir] if self.mode == "shadow" else ["-C", self.root]
        res = self.git("rev-parse", "--path-format=absolute", "--git-common-dir")
        if res.returncode != 0:
            raise Failure(2, "not a git repo: " + " ".join(self.prefix) + ": " + res.stderr.strip())
        self.common_dir = res.stdout.strip()

    def git(self, *args):
        return run_git(list(args), self.prefix)

    def out(self, *args):
        res = self.git(*args)
        if res.returncode != 0:
            raise Failure(1, "git " + " ".join(args) + " failed: " + res.stderr.strip())
        return res.stdout

    def sha(self, ref):
        res = self.git("rev-parse", "--verify", "--quiet", ref + "^{commit}")
        return res.stdout.strip() if res.returncode == 0 else None

    def worktrees(self):
        """git worktree list --porcelain as [{"path", "branch", "locked"}]."""
        found = []
        for block in self.out("worktree", "list", "--porcelain").split("\n\n"):
            lines = block.splitlines()
            if not lines or not lines[0].startswith("worktree "):
                continue
            entry = {"path": lines[0][len("worktree "):], "branch": None, "locked": False}
            for line in lines[1:]:
                if line.startswith("branch refs/heads/"):
                    entry["branch"] = line[len("branch refs/heads/"):]
                elif line == "locked" or line.startswith("locked "):
                    entry["locked"] = True
            found.append(entry)
        return found

    def restore_prefix(self):
        """The git prefix restore.md uses, shell-quoted."""
        return " ".join(shlex.quote(a) for a in self.prefix)


def ensure_archived(m, hdir):
    """The run folder of an archived run; raises Failure 2 or 3 otherwise."""
    try:
        index = _history.read_index(hdir)
        run_id, ledger_dir = _history.run_key(m)
    except _history.HistoryError as e:
        raise Failure(2, str(e))
    entry = _history.find_run(index, run_id, ledger_dir)
    if entry is None or not isinstance(entry.get("folder"), str) or not entry["folder"]:
        raise Failure(3, "run " + run_id + " is not archived in " + hdir
                      + " (no index.json entry); run archive-run first")
    # The index is data: a folder name that leaves the history dir ('..',
    # an absolute or a drive path) would put the restore point elsewhere.
    name = slash(entry["folder"])
    folder = hdir.rstrip("/") + "/" + name.strip("/")
    if (name.startswith("/") or re.match(r"^[A-Za-z]:", name) or ".." in name.split("/")
            or not _history.inside(folder, hdir) or same_place(folder, hdir)):
        raise Failure(2, "the index entry of run " + run_id + " in " + hdir + " has a bad folder: "
                      + json.dumps(entry["folder"]))
    if not os.path.isdir(folder):
        raise Failure(3, "run " + run_id + " is not archived: its folder " + folder + " is missing")
    return folder


def active_run(*args):
    """bash <scripts>/active-run args...: the completed process. Raises
    _shell.BashNotFound when there is no bash to run it with."""
    argv = _shell.bash_argv(os.path.join(SCRIPTS, "active-run"), *args)
    return subprocess.run(argv, capture_output=True, text=True, encoding="utf-8", errors="replace")


def ensure_inactive(run_id):
    try:
        res = active_run("list")
    except _shell.BashNotFound as e:
        raise Failure(3, "cannot check the active-run markers: " + str(e))
    try:
        markers = json.loads(res.stdout) if res.returncode == 0 else None
    except ValueError:
        markers = None
    if not isinstance(markers, list):
        raise Failure(3, "cannot check the active-run markers: active-run list exited "
                      + str(res.returncode) + ": " + res.stderr.strip())
    for marker in markers:
        if isinstance(marker, dict) and marker.get("run_id") == run_id:
            raise Failure(3, "run " + run_id + " has an active-run marker (status "
                          + str(marker.get("status")) + "): it can still be resumed. Remove the"
                          " marker only when the run is finished for good.")


def acquire_run_lock(m, manifest_path):
    """Take the run's launch lock, as a resume of the run does (active-run
    acquire <run_id> <manifest_path>); return its owner token."""
    run_id = m["run_id"]
    try:
        res = active_run("acquire", run_id, manifest_path)
    except _shell.BashNotFound as e:
        raise Failure(3, "cannot take the run lock of run " + run_id + ": " + str(e) + "; nothing was changed")
    if res.returncode == 4:
        raise Failure(3, "run " + run_id + " is held by another session (a resume or another cleanup);"
                      " nothing was changed")
    if res.returncode != 0:
        raise Failure(3, "cannot take the run lock of run " + run_id + ": active-run acquire exited "
                      + str(res.returncode) + ": " + res.stderr.strip() + "; nothing was changed")
    return res.stdout.strip()


def release_run_lock(run_id, token):
    """Give the run lock back and remove the marker acquire wrote (active-run
    release <run_id> --remove, which also deletes the run's checkout locks).
    A failure is only a warning: what cleanup did stands."""
    try:
        res = active_run("release", run_id, "--remove", "--owner", token)
        problem = None if res.returncode == 0 else ("active-run release exited " + str(res.returncode)
                                                    + ": " + res.stderr.strip())
    except _shell.BashNotFound as e:
        problem = str(e)
    if problem is not None:
        sys.stderr.write("cleanup: warning: cannot release the run lock of run " + run_id + " (" + problem
                         + "); once no session runs it, remove it with active-run remove " + run_id
                         + " --takeover\n")


def take_checkout_lock(repo, run_id):
    """Take the checkout lock of the main checkout for run_id (git mode), so
    no other run's setup can switch it while cleanup works."""
    try:
        _locks.checkout_lock(repo.root, run_id)
    except _locks.LockError as e:
        if e.code == 4 and e.run_id:
            raise Failure(3, "the checkout " + slash(repo.root) + " is in use by run " + e.run_id
                          + "; nothing was changed")
        raise Failure(3 if e.code == 4 else e.code, str(e))


def owned_worktree(repo, listing, path, branch):
    """The worktree list entry when path is a worktree of this repo on branch."""
    if os.path.islink(path) or not os.path.isdir(path):
        return None
    entry = next((e for e in listing if same_place(e["path"], path)), None)
    if entry is None or entry["branch"] != branch:
        return None
    res = run_git(["rev-parse", "--path-format=absolute", "--git-common-dir"], ["-C", path])
    if res.returncode != 0 or not same_place(res.stdout.strip(), repo.common_dir):
        return None
    return entry


def worktree_head(path):
    """(sha, None) for the worktree's HEAD, or (None, the git error)."""
    res = run_git(["rev-parse", "--verify", "HEAD"], ["-C", path])
    if res.returncode != 0 or not res.stdout.strip():
        return None, git_error(res)
    return res.stdout.strip(), None


def worktree_item(repo, entry, path, branch):
    head, error = worktree_head(path)
    item = {"path": path, "branch": branch, "head": head}
    if head is None:
        return dict(item, action="keep", reason="cannot read its HEAD: " + error)
    if entry["locked"]:
        return dict(item, action="keep", reason="the worktree is locked")
    res = run_git(STATUS, ["-C", path])
    if res.returncode != 0:
        return dict(item, action="keep", reason="git status failed: " + res.stderr.strip())
    if res.stdout.strip():
        return dict(item, action="keep", reason="it has uncommitted or untracked changes")
    return dict(item, action="remove", reason="clean and unlocked")


def recheck_worktree(repo, w):
    """Why the planned worktree w must be kept now, or None: called right
    before it is removed, it checks again that it is still this run's
    worktree on its branch, unlocked, at the planned HEAD and clean."""
    def changed(what):
        return "changed after the plan (" + what + "); run cleanup again"

    try:
        listing = repo.worktrees()
    except Failure as e:
        return changed(str(e))
    entry = owned_worktree(repo, listing, w["path"], w["branch"])
    if entry is None:
        return changed("it is no longer a worktree of this repo on " + w["branch"])
    if entry["locked"]:
        return changed("it is locked now")
    head, error = worktree_head(w["path"])
    if head is None:
        return changed("cannot read its HEAD: " + error)
    if head != w.get("head"):
        return changed("its HEAD moved from " + str(w.get("head"))[:12] + " to " + head[:12])
    res = run_git(STATUS, ["-C", w["path"]])
    if res.returncode != 0:
        return changed("git status failed: " + git_error(res))
    if res.stdout.strip():
        return changed("it has uncommitted or untracked changes")
    return None


def lane_branch_item(repo, branch, sha, kept_at, head):
    item = {"branch": branch, "sha": sha}
    if repo.mode == "shadow":
        return dict(item, action="keep", reason="shadow mode keeps every branch")
    if branch in kept_at:
        return dict(item, action="keep", reason="it is checked out in the kept worktree " + kept_at[branch])
    if head is None or repo.git("merge-base", "--is-ancestor", sha, head).returncode != 0:
        return dict(item, action="keep", reason="it is not merged into the main checkout's HEAD")
    return dict(item, action="remove", reason="merged into the main checkout's HEAD; deleted with git branch -d")


def feature_item(repo, m, sha):
    """The feature branch's item and the steps for it."""
    repo_cfg = m["repo"]
    branch, base = repo_cfg["branch"], repo_cfg["base_ref"]
    item = {"branch": branch, "sha": sha}
    if repo.mode == "shadow":
        return (dict(item, action="keep", reason="shadow mode keeps every branch and the shadow repo"),
                ["keep " + branch + ": shadow mode keeps every branch and the shadow repo"])
    reason, remote, merge = feature_precheck(repo, branch, base)
    steps = [
        "check that the main checkout " + slash(repo.root) + " is on " + branch + " and clean",
        "git fetch " + (remote or "<remote>") + " " + (merge or base),
        "check that " + branch + " is an ancestor of the fetched tip (the PR is merged)",
        "check that " + base + " is an ancestor of the fetched tip (a fast-forward)",
        "git switch " + base,
        "git merge --ff-only <fetched tip>",
        "git branch -d " + branch,
        "stop at the first failed check, leaving the checkout and " + branch + " as they are",
    ]
    if reason is None:
        return (dict(item, action="remove",
                     reason="if the fetched " + remote + " " + merge + " contains it (the PR is merged)"
                     " and " + base + " fast-forwards to it; otherwise it is kept"), steps)
    return dict(item, action="keep", reason=reason), steps


def feature_precheck(repo, branch, base):
    """(reason, remote, merge): why the git-mode feature branch must stay as
    it is before anything is fetched, or None; and base's upstream."""
    current = repo.git("symbolic-ref", "--quiet", "--short", "HEAD").stdout.strip()
    remote = repo.git("config", "branch." + base + ".remote").stdout.strip()
    merge = repo.git("config", "branch." + base + ".merge").stdout.strip()
    reason = None
    status = repo.git(*STATUS) if current == branch else None
    if current != branch:
        reason = "the main checkout is on " + (current or "a detached HEAD") + ", not " + branch
    elif status.returncode != 0:
        reason = "git status failed on the main checkout: " + status.stderr.strip()
    elif status.stdout.strip():
        reason = "the main checkout has uncommitted or untracked changes"
    elif repo.sha("refs/heads/" + base) is None:
        reason = "base_ref " + base + " is not a local branch"
    elif not remote or not merge:
        reason = base + " has no upstream to fetch"
    return reason, remote, merge


def make_plan(repo, m, run_folder):
    run_id, repo_cfg = m["run_id"], m["repo"]
    listing = repo.worktrees()
    owned = []
    for lane in m["lanes"]:
        owned.append((repo.worktree_root + "/lane-" + lane["id"], "pl-" + run_id + "-" + lane["id"]))
    if repo.mode == "shadow":
        owned.append((repo.worktree_root + "/feature", repo_cfg["branch"]))

    worktrees, owned_paths = [], []
    for path, branch in owned:
        entry = owned_worktree(repo, listing, path, branch)
        if entry is not None:
            worktrees.append(worktree_item(repo, entry, slash(path), branch))
            owned_paths.append(path)
    foreign = []
    if os.path.isdir(repo.worktree_root):
        for name in sorted(os.listdir(repo.worktree_root)):
            path = repo.worktree_root + "/" + name
            if not any(same_place(path, p) for p in owned_paths):
                foreign.append({"path": slash(path), "reason": NOT_OWNED})

    # A branch checked out in a worktree that stays cannot be deleted.
    removed = [w["path"] for w in worktrees if w["action"] == "remove"]
    kept_at = {}
    for e in listing:
        if e["branch"] and not any(same_place(e["path"], p) for p in removed):
            kept_at.setdefault(e["branch"], slash(e["path"]))
    head = repo.sha("HEAD") if repo.mode == "git" else None
    branches = []
    for lane in m["lanes"]:
        branch = "pl-" + run_id + "-" + lane["id"]
        sha = repo.sha("refs/heads/" + branch)
        if sha is not None:
            branches.append(lane_branch_item(repo, branch, sha, kept_at, head))
    feature_steps = []
    sha = repo.sha("refs/heads/" + repo_cfg["branch"])
    if sha is not None:
        item, feature_steps = feature_item(repo, m, sha)
        branches.append(item)

    refs = []
    listed = repo.out("for-each-ref", "--format=%(refname) %(objectname)", "refs/parallel-lanes/" + run_id)
    for line in listed.splitlines():
        ref, _, ref_sha = line.partition(" ")
        if ref:
            refs.append({"ref": ref, "sha": ref_sha, "action": "keep",
                         "reason": "cleanup never deletes refs/parallel-lanes refs"})
    return {
        "run_id": run_id, "mode": repo.mode, "run_folder": run_folder,
        "worktrees": worktrees, "branches": branches, "feature_steps": feature_steps,
        "refs": refs, "foreign": foreign, "restore_point": None,
    }


def new_folder(parent, stamp):
    """Create and return a new folder parent/stamp, or stamp-2, stamp-3, ..."""
    os.makedirs(parent, exist_ok=True)
    n = 1
    while True:
        path = parent + "/" + (stamp if n == 1 else stamp + "-" + str(n))
        try:
            os.mkdir(path)
            return path
        except FileExistsError:
            n += 1


def write_restore_point(repo, plan, run_folder):
    """Write and verify the restore point; return its folder. Failure 4 if not."""
    stamp = os.environ.get("PL_CLEANUP_STAMP") or time.strftime("%Y%m%dT%H%M%SZ", time.gmtime())
    if not STAMP.fullmatch(stamp):
        raise Failure(2, "PL_CLEANUP_STAMP must be a plain folder name, not " + repr(stamp))
    saved = {}
    for b in plan["branches"]:
        saved["refs/heads/" + b["branch"]] = b["sha"]
    for r in plan["refs"]:
        saved[r["ref"]] = r["sha"]
    try:
        folder = new_folder(run_folder + "/cleanup", stamp)
        _shell.write_text(folder + "/refs.json", json.dumps(saved, indent=2, sort_keys=True) + "\n")
    except OSError as e:
        raise Failure(4, "cannot write the restore point in " + run_folder + "/cleanup: " + str(e))
    bundle = folder + "/run.bundle"
    if saved:
        for args in (["bundle", "create", bundle, *sorted(saved)], ["bundle", "verify", bundle]):
            res = repo.git(*args)
            if res.returncode != 0:
                raise Failure(4, "git " + args[0] + " " + args[1] + " failed for the restore point "
                              + folder + ": " + res.stderr.strip() + "; nothing was removed")
    git = "git " + repo.restore_prefix()
    lines = [
        "# Restore point for run " + plan["run_id"],
        "",
        "Written by cleanup before it removed anything. refs.json lists every ref",
        "below with the commit it pointed at; run.bundle holds them all.",
        "",
        "## Refs",
        "",
        "Bring a ref back from the bundle (git refuses to fetch into a branch a",
        "worktree has checked out):",
        "",
        "```bash",
    ]
    lines += [git + " fetch " + shlex.quote(bundle) + " " + shlex.quote(ref + ":" + ref) for ref in sorted(saved)]
    if not saved:
        lines.append("# no run refs existed, so there is nothing to restore")
    lines += ["```", "", "## Worktrees", "", "Recreate a removed worktree once its branch is back:", "", "```bash"]
    removed = [w for w in plan["worktrees"] if w["action"] == "remove"]
    lines += [git + " worktree add " + shlex.quote(w["path"]) + " " + shlex.quote(w["branch"]) for w in removed]
    if not removed:
        lines.append("# no worktree is removed")
    lines += ["```", ""]
    try:
        _shell.write_text(folder + "/restore.md", "\n".join(lines))
    except OSError as e:
        raise Failure(4, "cannot write " + folder + "/restore.md: " + str(e) + "; nothing was removed")
    return folder


def git_error(res):
    return (res.stderr.strip() or res.stdout.strip() or "exit " + str(res.returncode)).replace("\n", " ")


def is_ancestor(repo, older, newer):
    """True or False, or None when git merge-base cannot tell."""
    code = repo.git("merge-base", "--is-ancestor", older, newer).returncode
    return {0: True, 1: False}.get(code)


def fetch(repo, remote, merge):
    """git fetch <remote> <merge>, bounded by FETCH_TIMEOUT_S: the completed
    process, or None when it timed out (its whole process tree is killed,
    as doctor's _command does, so a transport git started cannot keep it
    waiting). It never waits for a credential prompt."""
    env = dict(ENV)
    env["GCM_INTERACTIVE"] = "never"
    tree = sys.platform != "win32"
    argv = ["git", *repo.prefix, "fetch", remote, merge]
    try:
        proc = subprocess.Popen(argv, stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL, stdout=subprocess.PIPE, stderr=subprocess.PIPE,
                                text=True, encoding="utf-8", errors="surrogateescape", env=env,
                                start_new_session=tree)
    except OSError as e:
        return subprocess.CompletedProcess(argv, 127, "", str(e))
    try:
        out, err = proc.communicate(timeout=FETCH_TIMEOUT_S)
    except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:
        _doctor._kill_tree(proc)
        return None
    return subprocess.CompletedProcess(argv, proc.returncode, out or "", err or "")


def remove_feature(repo, m, planned):
    """Switch the main checkout to the base, fast-forward it to the fetched
    upstream tip and delete the feature branch: (removed, reason). Stops at
    the first failed condition, leaving the checkout and the branch. The
    branch must still be at planned, its tip in the plan."""
    branch, base = m["repo"]["branch"], m["repo"]["base_ref"]
    if repo.sha("refs/heads/" + branch) is None:
        return False, GONE
    reason, remote, merge = feature_precheck(repo, branch, base)
    if reason is not None:
        return False, reason
    fetched = "the fetched " + remote + " " + merge
    res = fetch(repo, remote, merge)
    if res is None:
        return False, ("git fetch " + remote + " " + merge + " timed out after " + str(FETCH_TIMEOUT_S)
                       + " s (a stalled network, or a credential prompt nobody answers)")
    if res.returncode != 0:
        return False, "git fetch " + remote + " " + merge + " failed: " + git_error(res)
    tip = repo.sha("FETCH_HEAD")
    if tip is None:
        return False, "git fetch " + remote + " " + merge + " gave no commit"
    fetched += " (" + tip[:12] + ")"
    merged = is_ancestor(repo, "refs/heads/" + branch, tip)
    if merged is None:
        return False, "git merge-base could not compare " + branch + " with " + fetched
    if not merged:
        return False, ("it is not merged into " + fetched + ": the PR is not merged yet (or was squashed"
                       " or rebased); run cleanup again after it is")
    ff = is_ancestor(repo, "refs/heads/" + base, tip)
    if ff is None:
        return False, "git merge-base could not compare " + base + " with " + fetched
    if not ff:
        return False, base + " cannot fast-forward to " + fetched + ": it has commits the upstream does not"
    current = repo.sha("refs/heads/" + branch)
    if current is None:
        return False, GONE
    if current != planned:
        return False, MOVED
    res = repo.git("switch", base)
    if res.returncode != 0:
        return False, "git switch " + base + " failed: " + git_error(res)
    res = repo.git("merge", "--ff-only", tip)
    if res.returncode != 0:
        return False, ("the main checkout is now on " + base + ", but git merge --ff-only " + tip[:12]
                       + " failed: " + git_error(res))
    done = "switched the main checkout to " + base + " and fast-forwarded it to " + fetched
    res = repo.git("branch", "-d", branch)
    if res.returncode != 0:
        return False, done + "; git branch -d refused: " + git_error(res)
    return True, "merged into " + fetched + "; " + done + ", then deleted it with git branch -d"


def remove_owned(repo, m, plan):
    """Remove what the plan marks remove, in order; return (removed, kept)."""
    removed, kept = [], []

    def note(ok, entry, reason):
        (removed if ok else kept).append(dict(entry, reason=reason))

    # 1. Run-owned worktrees. git worktree remove checks again that each is
    # clean and unlocked, and refuses otherwise; its own git status would
    # follow status.showUntrackedFiles, so it is told to show them all.
    # Each is checked again first (recheck_worktree); one that changed
    # after the plan is kept, and so is its planned branch.
    still_out = {}
    for w in plan["worktrees"]:
        entry = {"kind": "worktree", "path": w["path"], "branch": w["branch"]}
        if w["action"] != "remove":
            note(False, entry, w["reason"])
            continue
        reason = recheck_worktree(repo, w)
        if reason is not None:
            note(False, entry, reason)
            still_out[w["branch"]] = "its worktree " + w["path"] + " " + reason
            continue
        res = repo.git("-c", "status.showUntrackedFiles=all", "worktree", "remove", w["path"])
        if res.returncode != 0:
            note(False, entry, "git worktree remove refused: " + git_error(res))
            still_out[w["branch"]] = "it is checked out in the kept worktree " + w["path"]
        else:
            note(True, entry, w["reason"])
    for f in plan["foreign"]:
        note(False, {"kind": "path", "path": f["path"]}, f["reason"])

    # 2. Lane branches, then 3. the feature branch.
    feature = m["repo"]["branch"]
    for b in plan["branches"]:
        entry = {"kind": "branch", "branch": b["branch"], "sha": b["sha"]}
        if b["action"] != "remove":
            note(False, entry, b["reason"])
        elif b["branch"] == feature:
            continue
        elif b["branch"] in still_out:
            note(False, entry, still_out[b["branch"]])
        elif repo.sha("refs/heads/" + b["branch"]) is None:
            note(False, entry, GONE)
        elif repo.sha("refs/heads/" + b["branch"]) != b["sha"]:
            note(False, entry, MOVED)
        else:
            res = repo.git("branch", "-d", b["branch"])
            if res.returncode != 0:
                note(False, entry, "git branch -d refused: " + git_error(res))
            else:
                note(True, entry, b["reason"])
    for b in plan["branches"]:
        if b["branch"] == feature and b["action"] == "remove":
            ok, reason = remove_feature(repo, m, b["sha"])
            note(ok, {"kind": "branch", "branch": b["branch"], "sha": b["sha"]}, reason)
    for r in plan["refs"]:
        note(False, {"kind": "ref", "ref": r["ref"], "sha": r["sha"]}, r["reason"])

    # 4. The worktree root, only when nothing is left in it.
    root = repo.worktree_root
    entry = {"kind": "worktree_root", "path": slash(root)}
    if os.path.isdir(root) and not os.path.islink(root):
        try:
            left = os.listdir(root)
            if left:
                note(False, entry, "it is not empty (" + str(len(left)) + " item"
                     + ("" if len(left) == 1 else "s") + " left)")
            else:
                os.rmdir(root)
                note(True, entry, "empty after the run-owned worktrees were removed")
        except OSError as e:
            note(False, entry, "rmdir failed: " + str(e))
    if repo.mode == "shadow":
        note(False, {"kind": "shadow_repo", "path": slash(repo.git_dir)},
             "shadow mode keeps the shadow repo; remove it with shadow remove when it is no longer needed")
    return removed, kept


def item_name(item):
    if item["kind"] == "worktree":
        return item["path"] + " (" + item["branch"] + ")"
    if item["kind"] in ("branch", "ref"):
        return item[item["kind"]] + " " + item["sha"][:12]
    return item["path"]


def render_done(plan):
    out = ["cleanup of run " + plan["run_id"] + " (" + plan["mode"] + " mode)",
           "run folder: " + plan["run_folder"], "", "removed:"]
    out += ["  " + i["kind"] + "  " + item_name(i) + ": " + i["reason"] for i in plan["removed"]] or ["  (nothing)"]
    out += ["", "kept:"]
    out += ["  " + i["kind"] + "  " + item_name(i) + ": " + i["reason"] for i in plan["kept"]] or ["  (nothing)"]
    out += ["", "restore point: " + plan["restore_point"],
            "(its restore.md has the commands that bring each removed branch and worktree back)"]
    return "\n".join(out) + "\n"


def render(plan):
    out = ["cleanup plan for run " + plan["run_id"] + " (" + plan["mode"] + " mode)",
           "run folder: " + plan["run_folder"], "", "worktrees:"]
    out += ["  " + w["action"] + "  " + w["path"] + " (" + w["branch"] + "): " + w["reason"]
            for w in plan["worktrees"]] or ["  (no run-owned worktree)"]
    out += ["", "branches:"]
    out += ["  " + b["action"] + "  " + b["branch"] + " " + b["sha"][:12] + ": " + b["reason"]
            for b in plan["branches"]] or ["  (no run branch)"]
    if plan["feature_steps"]:
        out += ["", "feature branch steps:"]
        out += ["  " + str(i) + ". " + s for i, s in enumerate(plan["feature_steps"], 1)]
    if plan["refs"]:
        out += ["", "refs:"]
        out += ["  keep  " + r["ref"] + " " + r["sha"][:12] + ": " + r["reason"] for r in plan["refs"]]
    out += ["", "left in place under the worktree root:"]
    out += ["  " + f["path"] + ": " + f["reason"] for f in plan["foreign"]] or ["  (nothing else)"]
    out.append("")
    if plan["restore_point"]:
        out.append("restore point: " + plan["restore_point"])
    else:
        out.append("Nothing was changed. Run again with --yes to write a restore point and clean up.")
    return "\n".join(out) + "\n"


def main():
    _shell.setup_io()
    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(prog="cleanup", description="Tidy up after an archived run.")
    parser.add_argument("manifest")
    parser.add_argument("--yes", action="store_true", help="write the restore point, then remove")
    parser.add_argument("--json", action="store_true", help="print the plan as JSON")
    parser.add_argument("--history-dir", help="the history dir (default: _history.history_dir())")
    args = parser.parse_args()
    try:
        m = load_manifest(args.manifest)
        try:
            hdir = _history.history_dir(args.history_dir)
        except _shell.BashNotFound as e:
            raise Failure(2, str(e))
        run_folder = ensure_archived(m, hdir)
        ensure_inactive(m["run_id"])
        repo = Repo(m)
        plan = make_plan(repo, m, run_folder)
        if args.yes:
            # What changes between the plan and the locks is caught by the
            # rechecks right before each removal.
            token = acquire_run_lock(m, args.manifest)
            try:
                if repo.mode == "git":
                    take_checkout_lock(repo, m["run_id"])
                plan["restore_point"] = write_restore_point(repo, plan, run_folder)
                plan["removed"], plan["kept"] = remove_owned(repo, m, plan)
            finally:
                release_run_lock(m["run_id"], token)
    except Failure as e:
        sys.stderr.write("cleanup: " + str(e) + "\n")
        return e.code
    if args.json:
        sys.stdout.write(json.dumps(plan, indent=2) + "\n")
    else:
        sys.stdout.write(render_done(plan) if args.yes else render(plan))
    return 0


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main())
